From 7fa89979b42265dc82312267f53c1dc8aae121c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TranAnhDuy123 <tranminhhuyen22@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:56:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Plane: INDI body-rate loop for lift motors and control
 surfaces

Q_INDI_ENABLE=0 (default) allocates the stock AC_AttitudeControl_TS and
leaves every stock code path unchanged.

With Q_INDI_ENABLE=1:
- AC_AttitudeControl_INDI (subclass of AC_AttitudeControl_TS) runs INDI
  on the axes in Q_INDI_AXES with non-zero effectiveness while the lift
  motors are spooled up; other axes keep the stock PID. The fed-back
  effector state is the roll/pitch input the mixer actually applied,
  recovered from the motor outputs.
- AP_FW_Controller runs INDI on aileron/elevator in fixed-wing flight
  proper (transition complete, no assist, not a VTOL mode), with
  effectiveness scaled by 1/speed_scaler^2.
- The effector feedback passes through the same filters and delays as
  the angular-acceleration estimate (actuator model, backward-difference
  half sample, INS gyro low-pass, INDI low-pass).
- New logs INDI (VTOL) and INDF (fixed wing).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
